From ddc1f6c0ac37cf52c886777dc8651838e3e5d7a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 11:49:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(inventory): confirm survival offhand transfers from
 Bedrock
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Bedrock 2193 rejects Java cursor-to-offhand item stack requests, while a normal player UI to offhand inventory transaction is accepted. Send that transaction only for an empty offhand slot, then clear Java’s cursor only after Bedrock reports the matching item and count in offhand. Bedrock assigns a new stack net ID during this move, so the completion check uses item data rather than requiring the old ID. Timeout recovery reopens inventory and waits for authoritative cursor and offhand contents.
